 "note": "The press-two-tabs latch, v6, battery side only: one push latches it, one squeeze unlatches it and holds the pack on the grabber. Cut at the tab line; the +x slider and blade are in section, the -x ones whole. Two steel springs between the tabs (2.33 N at rest, 2.21 x the 35 g inertia of a slider; 4.66 N squeezed). The grabber grips the cartridge, not the loose tabs: each blade's nub slides onto a 10 deg wedge foot on the centre rib (self-locking) and draws the cartridge onto four heel pads; at 8 N per blade 13.21 N on the pads, x3.2 / x3.72 against tipping / slip at 1 g in the worst direction. Receiver, XT60 carrier, guide poles, steel bolt pins and the 20 deg seat ramp are v5's. Built by parts/latch6/make.py on the vendored latch v4 CAD.",
 "cg_ref": null,
